{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implementation will be in Go, extending the existing Hyperledger Fabric configuration library (e.g., configtx / config library).",
    "API design will follow existing library patterns, using strongly typed Go structs and standard error handling routines.",
    "Capability manipulation functions (U5) will support both explicit helper functions/toggles and standard capability setters/deleters to allow managing unknown or custom capabilities cleanly.",
    "Examples will be implemented as Go executable example tests (`Example...` functions) ensuring they act as both runnable documentation and automated tests."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The core protobuf data structures and basic config update generation mechanisms (`configtx.Compute`) already exist in the codebase.",
    "No external network dependencies are required for unit and example tests; mock or sample protobuf config blocks can be generated in memory.",
    "All work is carried out by a single software engineer familiar with Go and Hyperledger Fabric channel configuration structures."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Development Setup & Specification Analysis",
      "activity_description": "Set up the local development environment, analyze existing configuration parser/builder structures, and plan function signatures for missing helper functions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Orderer Endpoint Config Modification (U1, U2)",
      "activity_description": "Implement functions to add and remove orderer endpoints from an orderer organization's configuration group, including standard validation and protobuf updates, with unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Organization Policy Retrieval Helper (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Implement a helper function to inspect and retrieve policies for a specified organization (Application, Orderer, or Consortium), along with unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Capabilities Inspection and Modification API (U4, U5)",
      "activity_description": "Implement capability retrieval functions for orderer, application, and channel capabilities returning `config.Capabilities`, and implement functions/toggles to add and remove capabilities, along with unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Application Config Retrieval & ACL Updates (U6, U7)",
      "activity_description": "Implement functions to retrieve existing application configuration (`config.Application`) and to add/remove ACLs from an application group, along with unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Example Test Suite Refactoring & Modularization (U8 & Examples)",
      "activity_description": "Refactor the giant end-to-end example into smaller, focused example tests demonstrating orderer updates, application updates, organization management, MSP modifications, and capability changes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Integration Testing, Validation & Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Perform full test suite execution, verify all acceptance criteria across U1-U8, refine code documentation, and prepare the pull request.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 9.5
  }
}
```

